{
  "reasons": {
    "added-isa": "Brenton's English adds it to make a Greek phrase English (or from the Hebrew), and the Greek verse has no word for it ('works' of 2:8's 'the works which', 'yourselves' of 2:10, 'high' of 2:14, 'in order to' of 2:20, 'concerning' of 5:1, 'book' of 8:1, 'how to call' of 8:4, 'gates' of 13:2, 'a day of' of 13:9, 'ways; howl' of 15:3); each was read against its verse and no Greek word of a neighbouring chunk renders it (mw-u2w5klk.349.14).",
    "other-verse-isa": "Brenton's English of the verse carries a clause whose Greek words are in the next or the verse before (Swete's verse division differs from LXX2012's): 3:9's 'Therefore now their glory has been brought low,' is the end of Swete's 3:8, 3:10's 'Woe to their soul, for they have devised an evil counsel against themselves,' the end of Swete's 3:9, 3:17's 'in that day' the start of 3:18, and 3:21 to 3:24 hold the English of Swete's 3:22 to 3:26 (the garments, the sweet smell and the girdle, the sword and the stores of ornaments) while the Greek words of those verses have no English chunk to point at; 6:8's 'said, Go, and say to this people,' is the first words of Swete's 6:9, and 18:3's 'the rivers of the land' the end of 18:2 (mw-u2w5klk.349.14).",
    "pair-isa": "The Greek word that renders it is a pair the aligner made to another English word, which the model pass does not touch and no fix row could move without taking another word's Greek ('enter' of 3:13 on στήσει's 'stand', 'fire' of 3:14 on ἐνεπυρίσατε's 'set', 'king' and 'side' of 7:6 on βασιλεύσομεν's 'make' and ἡμᾶς's 'we', 'believe' of 7:9 on πιστεύσητε's 'neither', 'whoever' of 13:15 on ὃς's 'that', 'far off' of 6:12 beside 'remove' for the one word μακρυνεῖ) (mw-u2w5klk.349.14).",
    "hebrew-13-21": "Brenton's last line of 13:21 ('and satyrs shall dwell there; and hedgehogs shall make their nests in their houses. It will come soon, and will not wait.') translates the Hebrew; Swete's Greek of the verse ends at 'and devils shall dance there' (mw-u2w5klk.349.14)."
  },
